{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"The level has two selectable pieces: one vertical and one horizontal. Clicking switches control, and each arrow moves the selected piece by three pixels. The other shapes have stayed in place so far. I’ll test the narrow passages and pushing behavior to see how the pieces can reach the three outlines."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > probe_routes.py <<'PY'\nfrom probe7 import entry\nimport gkm_arena as A\nimport perception as P\n\ndef brief(e):\n return [(b.color,b.bbox) for b in P.connected_components(e.frame(),colors=(11,14))]\ndef test(e,actions):\n c=e.clone()\n for a,n in actions:\n  for _ in range(n): P.safe_step(c,a)\n  print(a,n,brief(c),'level',c.levels_completed)\n return c\n\ndef probe(e):\n entry(e)\n print('HORIZONTAL')\n c=test(e,[((6,35,52),1),(3,3),(1,7),(3,5),(1,8),(4,1),(2,12)])\n print('VERTICAL')\n test(e,[(1,10),(3,3),(1,5),(3,6),(2,6)])\nprint(A.run_program('ka59',probe)[::2])\nPY\npython probe_routes.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
